        "subject": "LU-21228 lfs: find --report",
        "message": "LU-21228 lfs: find --report\n\nAdd --report to lfs find, so that a search can describe a filesystem\nas well as list it: a YAML document in the style of job_stats, with\nhistograms of size, space and age, and the largest directories.\n\n--report[=FILE] is an action, as -fprint is in find(1): the report\ngoes to FILE, to a file under /var/log/lustre, or with --report=- to\nstdout.  A target scan reports what it read and what the options\nmatched.\n\nA file without strict size-on-MDT takes its size and space from the\nlazy size-on-MDT.  The report prints totals, so a slightly stale LSOM\nis good enough, and no OST needs to be read.\n\nA walk stats each size the MDT did not give, or takes the lazy size\nwith --lazy.  --report-memory limits the report's tables, --no-report\ncancels --report, and --report-format names the format (yaml).  With\n--fid2path a report-only search names directories through the mount.\nA report covers one filesystem, since its tables are keyed by FID.\n\nPrograms get the same report from llapi_find_report(), and note a\ntarget they skipped with llapi_find_report_note().\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iee4d0eda464f1c050a31e50492663632d999cc6d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
